From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:04:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=2, a model paged to the
 card by use

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch). ggml-sycl's system
allocations (GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=1: a buffer of 4 GiB or more is host
memory the card reads through shared virtual memory) put the whole model
in video memory all the same: the load copies every tensor on the card,
and the first token rewrites every expert tensor whole. Measured on an
Intel Arc Pro B70 with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: 21.7 GiB in video memory by the
driver's count, of which the process's own counters show 3.2.

With the value 2 the weights of such a buffer are written from the host
and its expert tensors are not reordered, so a page reaches the card when
a kernel first reads it and the experts no token selects stay in host
memory. The value 1 is unchanged.

STAGED, for a measurement: not compiled where it was written, never run.
What it is for, and the rows that say whether it does it, are in
docs/notes/backend-qualification-2026-11-21.md (the Louise repository).

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 .../patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch | 86 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 86 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..22fdab6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0013-sycl-usm-system-by-use.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+sycl: GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=2 pages a system allocation to the card by use
+
+With GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=1 a buffer of 4 GiB or more is host memory the
+card reads through shared virtual memory - and yet the whole model is in
+video memory as soon as it is loaded (measured on an Arc Pro B70 with a
+22 GB mixture-of-experts model: 21.7 GiB by the driver's own count), for
+two reasons, both in this file:
+
+- the load writes every tensor with a copy that runs ON THE CARD
+  (set_tensor: stream->memcpy), so the card faults in every page;
+- the first token reorders each expert tensor whole (opt_for_reorder_id ->
+  reorder_qw), reading and rewriting every expert of every layer, the ones
+  no token selects included.
+
+GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=2 leaves both out for such a buffer: the weights are
+written from the host, and an expert tensor keeps the layout it was loaded
+in (the kernels take either layout). A page then reaches the card when a
+kernel first reads it; an expert no token selects stays in host memory.
+The dense weights are reordered as before - every token reads them.
+
+1 behaves as it did. 2 is for measuring: the expert kernels on the plain
+layout are the slower ones, and what the driver does with such pages when
+another process needs the card is its own policy.
+
+Not compiled where it was written (no SYCL compiler there): three small
+changes, each beside the code it guards.
+---
+diff --git a/docs/backend/SYCL.md b/docs/backend/SYCL.md
+index 8649fca..e6705b1 100644
+--- a/docs/backend/SYCL.md
++++ b/docs/backend/SYCL.md
+@@ -840,7 +840,7 @@ User can use the device management in [docs/multi-gpu.md](https://github.com/ggm
+ | GGML_SYCL_SPARSE_FA_MARGIN | [0,..] default:256 | Set the margin value for Sparse Flash-attention.|
+ | ZES_ENABLE_SYSMAN | 0 (default) or 1 | Support to get free memory of GPU by sycl::aspect::ext_intel_free_memory.<br>Recommended to use when --split-mode = layer |
+ | UR_L0_ENABLE_RELAXED_ALLOCATION_LIMITS | 0 (default) or 1 | Allow SYCL/Unified Runtime Level Zero device allocations larger than 4 GiB. llama.cpp's direct Level Zero allocation path requests the relaxed maximum-size limit itself when GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_LEVEL_ZERO=1. |
+-| GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM | 0 (default) or 1 | Enable experimental support for [USM system allocations](https://github.khronos.org/SYCL_Reference/iface/usm_basic_concept.html#system-allocations) for large GPU buffers. This requires enough host memory for model weights and caches, an Intel Xe2+ GPU such as BMG or newer and supported on Linux only, with CONFIG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM enabled. |
++| GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM | 0 (default), 1 or 2 | With 2, the buffer is paged to the GPU by use: weights are written from the host and expert tensors are not reordered, so a page reaches the GPU when a kernel first reads it and unselected experts stay in host memory (slower expert kernels; measure). With 1: enable experimental support for [USM system allocations](https://github.khronos.org/SYCL_Reference/iface/usm_basic_concept.html#system-allocations) for large GPU buffers. This requires enough host memory for model weights and caches, an Intel Xe2+ GPU such as BMG or newer and supported on Linux only, with CONFIG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM enabled. |
+ | GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK | 1 (default) or 0 | Workaround for BMG (Arc B-series) GPUs, where the Level Zero driver accepts device allocations beyond VRAM and moves the overflow to system RAM, which can exhaust host memory when a model does not fit (e.g. `-ngl 999`, see https://github.com/intel/compute-runtime/issues/1047). When enabled, a model or split buffer that does not fit in the device's free memory is refused and the model load fails with an error. Set to 0 to disable. |
+ 
+ 1. <a id="sycl-graph-footnote"></a>SYCL Graph support (`GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_GRAPH=1`) is limited to single-GPU workloads and may also depend on the model architecture and kernels in use.
+diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+index d3797f8..4888a11 100644
+--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
++++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+@@ -785,6 +785,15 @@ static bool ggml_backend_buffer_is_sycl(ggml_backend_buffer_t buffer) {
+     return buffer->buft->iface.get_name == ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_type_get_name;
+ }
+ 
++// GGML_SYCL_USM_SYSTEM=2: a system allocation is paged to the card BY USE. Its weights are written from the host
++// and no pass rewrites a whole expert tensor, so a page reaches the card when a kernel first reads it and the
++// experts no token selects stay in host memory. With =1 every page is written, and the experts rewritten, by
++// kernels on the card: the whole buffer is in video memory once the model is loaded and has answered.
++static bool ggml_sycl_buffer_paged_by_use(ggml_backend_buffer_t buffer) {
++    return g_ggml_sycl_usm_system >= 2 && buffer != nullptr && ggml_backend_buffer_is_sycl(buffer) &&
++           ((const ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_context *) buffer->context)->is_usm_system;
++}
++
+ static void
+ ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_free_buffer(ggml_backend_buffer_t buffer) try {
+     ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_context * ctx = ( ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_context *)buffer->context;
+@@ -882,6 +891,13 @@ static void ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_set_tensor(ggml_backend_buffer_t buffer,
+     ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_context * ctx = ( ggml_backend_sycl_buffer_context *)buffer->context;
+     ggml_sycl_set_device(ctx->device);
+ 
++    // paged by use: the buffer is host memory, written here from the host. A copy run on the card would fault
++    // every page of the model in at load
++    if (ggml_sycl_buffer_paged_by_use(buffer)) {
++        memcpy((char *) tensor->data + offset, data, size);
++        return;
++    }
++
+     // copy through pinned memory so the device never reads mmap()ed pages directly
+     // chunks pipeline on the in-order compute queue, so no drain per tensor is needed
+     if (ggml_sycl_buffer_init_staging(ctx)) {
+@@ -5090,6 +5106,11 @@ static void opt_for_reorder_id(ggml_backend_sycl_context * ctx, const ggml_tenso
+     if (!g_ggml_sycl_enable_optimize || !ctx->opt_feature.reorder) {
+         return;
+     }
++    // paged by use: the reorder reads and rewrites EVERY expert of the tensor on the card, which would bring them
++    // all in at the first token. The tensor keeps the layout it was loaded in; the kernels take either
++    if (ggml_sycl_buffer_paged_by_use(src0->buffer)) {
++        return;
++    }
+     if (src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q8_0 && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q3_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q4_K &&
+         src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q5_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_Q6_K && src0->type != GGML_TYPE_MXFP4) {
+         return;
